cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AZ-Eval: a parallel Azerbaijani-English benchmark"
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Garibli
    given-names: Nihat
    email: qaribli.nihat.nemat@bsu.edu.az
    affiliation: Baku State University
repository-code: "https://github.com/nihatgaribli/AZ-Eval"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22050776
version: v0.1.0
abstract: >-
  An open parallel Azerbaijani-English benchmark of 356 human-verified
  short-answer items, with an evaluation pipeline that separates knowledge
  from orthography through a chain of nested normalizations. Used to show
  that fine-tuning on Kazakh produces negative transfer to Azerbaijani,
  with a largely orthographic mechanism.
keywords:
  - low-resource evaluation
  - Azerbaijani
  - cross-lingual transfer
  - Turkic languages
  - writing systems
  - large language models
